.TH SUM 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
sum \- checksum files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sum
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sum
sums the contents of a file.
On maux the sum is a 16-bit rotating checksum: rotate right one bit,
add the next byte, and retain the low 16 bits.
For each file it prints the checksum, the number of 512-byte blocks
rounded upward, and the file name.
With no operands it reads standard input and omits the name.
An input which cannot be opened is reported and skipped.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/SUM  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cksum(1), cmp(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 if any input cannot be opened.
.SH BUGS
This checksum detects accidental changes; it is not a cryptographic digest. It is not the CRC used by cksum.
